msgstr "{{ bp_modular_design }}"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/back-propagation.md:293
msgid "每个操作只需要定义："
msgstr "Each operation only needs to define:"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/back-propagation.md:295
msgid "前向：如何计算输出"
msgstr "Forward: How to compute the output"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/back-propagation.md:296
msgid "反向：如何计算梯度"
msgstr "Backward: How to compute the gradient"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/back-propagation.md:298
msgid "这使得添加新操作变得简单。"
msgstr "This makes adding new operations straightforward."

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/back-propagation.md:300
msgid "常见问题"
msgstr "Frequently Asked Questions"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/back-propagation.md:303
msgid "梯度消失（Vanishing Gradient）"
msgstr "Vanishing Gradient"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/back-propagation.md:305
msgid "想象一个100层的神经网络。当你训练时，发现靠近输出层的参数更新正常，但靠近输入层的参数几乎不动——就像前面几十层\"冻住\"了一样。这就是**梯度消失**。"
msgstr "Imagine a 100-layer neural network. During training, you notice that parameters near the output layer update normally, but parameters near the input layer barely move—as if the first dozens of layers are \"frozen.\" This is the **vanishing gradient** problem."

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/back-propagation.md:307
msgid "为什么会发生？回顾链式法则：梯度是**各层影响的乘积**。如果每一层的梯度都小于1（比如Sigmoid在饱和区的梯度只有0.01），100层连乘后："
msgstr "Why does it happen? Recall the chain rule: gradients are the **product of effects at each layer**. If the gradient at each layer is less than 1 (for example, Sigmoid's gradient in the saturation region is only 0.01), after multiplying across 100 layers:"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/back-propagation.md:309
#, python-brace-format
msgid "0.01 \\times 0.01 \\times ... \\times 0.01 \\quad (100次) = 10^{-200}"
msgstr "0.01 \\times 0.01 \\times ... \\times 0.01 \\quad (100 \\text{ times}) = 10^{-200}"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/back-propagation.md:311
msgid "这个数小到计算机都当成0处理了！具体场景是：使用Sigmoid/Tanh激活函数时，输入值很大或很小会让函数进入\"饱和区\"，梯度接近0；网络层数越深，问题越严重。"
msgstr "This number is so small that computers treat it as 0! A typical scenario occurs when using Sigmoid/Tanh activation functions: large or small input values push the function into the \"saturation region,\" making the gradient close to 0; the deeper the network, the more severe the issue becomes."

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/back-propagation.md:313
msgid "**后果**：前面的层学不到东西，模型退化成\"浅层网络\"——只有后面几层在学习。对于图像数据，前面的层本应学习边缘、纹理等基础特征，但这些特征学不到。"
msgstr "**Consequences**: Earlier layers fail to learn anything, causing the model to degenerate into a \"shallow network\" where only the last few layers are learning. For image data, earlier layers are supposed to learn low-level features like edges and textures, but fail to acquire them."

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/back-propagation.md:315
#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/back-propagation.md:335
msgid "**解决方案**："
msgstr "**Solutions**:"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/back-propagation.md:316
#, python-brace-format
msgid "**ReLU激活函数**：正区间的梯度恒为1，不会衰减（见 {doc}`activation-functions`）"
msgstr "**ReLU activation function**: The gradient in the positive region is constantly 1 and does not decay (see {doc}`activation-functions`)"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/back-propagation.md:317
msgid "**批归一化（BatchNorm）**：控制每层的数值范围，避免进入饱和区"
msgstr "**Batch Normalization (BatchNorm)**: Controls the value range at each layer, preventing inputs from entering saturation regions"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/back-propagation.md:318
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**残差连接（ResNet）**：让梯度有\"捷径\"可以直达前面层（见 {doc}`../cnn-expedition/image-net-"
"era/res-net` 中的数学推导）"
msgstr ""
"**Residual connections (ResNet)**: Provides a \"shortcut\" for gradients to reach earlier layers directly "
"(see mathematical derivation in {doc}`../cnn-expedition/image-net-era/res-net`)"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/back-propagation.md:319
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**跳跃连接（U-Net）**：在编码器-解码器架构中保留梯度路径（见 {doc}`../unet-image-"
"segmentation/u-net`）"
msgstr ""
"**Skip connections (U-Net)**: Preserves gradient paths in encoder-decoder architectures "
"(see {doc}`../unet-image-segmentation/u-net`)"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/back-propagation.md:323
msgid "梯度爆炸（Exploding Gradient）"
msgstr "Exploding Gradient"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/back-propagation.md:325
msgid "训练过程中，损失突然变成NaN（不是数字），或者参数变得极其巨大（比如从0.1变成1000000），模型完全失控。这就是**梯度爆炸**。"
msgstr "During training, if the loss suddenly becomes NaN (Not a Number) or parameters grow extremely large (e.g., jumping from 0.1 to 1,000,000), the model spins completely out of control. This is an **exploding gradient**."

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/back-propagation.md:327
msgid "为什么会发生？和梯度消失相反，如果每层的梯度都大于1（比如权重初始化过大，梯度为2），100层连乘后："
msgstr "Why does it happen? Contrary to vanishing gradients, if the gradient at each layer is greater than 1 (for example, if weight initialization is too large and gradients are 2), after multiplying across 100 layers:"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/back-propagation.md:329
#, python-brace-format
msgid "2 \\times 2 \\times ... \\times 2 \\quad (100次) = 2^{100} \\approx 10^{30}"
msgstr "2 \\times 2 \\times ... \\times 2 \\quad (100) = 2^{100} \\approx 10^{30}"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/back-propagation.md:331
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"这是一个天文数字！参数会被更新得极其剧烈，完全偏离最优解。常见于权重初始化不当，或循环神经网络（RNN，详见 {ref}`rnn-"
"problems`）处理长序列时的梯度爆炸。"
msgstr ""
"This is an astronomical number! Parameters are updated drastically, completely diverging "
"from the optimal solution. It commonly occurs due to improper weight initialization, "
"or in recurrent neural networks (RNNs, see {ref}`rnn-problems` for details) handling long sequences."

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/back-propagation.md:333
msgid "**后果**：参数更新过大跳出最优解区域，损失函数震荡发散，甚至数值溢出（NaN）导致训练彻底失败。"
msgstr "**Consequences**: Parameter updates are too large, skipping over optimal regions, causing loss oscillation, divergence, or numerical overflow (NaN) that leads to complete training failure."

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/back-propagation.md:336
msgid "**梯度裁剪**：设定梯度上限，超过就截断"
msgstr "**Gradient Clipping**: Sets an upper threshold on gradients, truncating them if exceeded"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/back-propagation.md:337
msgid "**权重正则化（L2正则）**：惩罚过大的权重"
msgstr "**Weight Regularization (L2 Regularization)**: Penalizes excessively large weights"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/back-propagation.md:338
msgid "**更好的初始化**：如Xavier初始化、He初始化，控制初始梯度规模"
msgstr "**Better Initialization**: Such as Xavier initialization or He initialization to control initial gradient scale"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/back-propagation.md:339
msgid "**更小的学习率**：让参数更新更温和"
msgstr "**Smaller Learning Rate**: Makes parameter updates gentler"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/back-propagation.md:341
msgid "总结"
msgstr "Summary"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/back-propagation.md:343
msgid "反向传播是深度学习的核心算法："
msgstr "Backpropagation is a core algorithm in deep learning:"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/back-propagation.md:345
msgid "**信用分配**：将最终损失\"分摊\"给每个参数"
msgstr "**Credit Assignment**: \"Apportions\" the final loss to each parameter"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/back-propagation.md:346
#, python-brace-format
msgid "**链式法则**：梯度从输出层逐层回传（基于 {doc}`computational-graph` 的结构）"
msgstr "**Chain Rule**: Gradients flow backward layer by layer from the output layer (based on the structure of the {doc}`computational-graph`)"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/back-propagation.md:347
msgid "**高效计算**：复用中间结果，时间与网络规模线性相关"
msgstr "**Efficient Computation**: Reuses intermediate results, with time complexity linear in network size"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/back-propagation.md:349
#, python-brace-format
msgid "反向传播计算出的梯度用于更新模型参数。下一节 {doc}`gradient-descent` 将详细介绍如何利用这些梯度进行参数优化。"
msgstr "Gradients computed by backpropagation are used to update model parameters. The next section, {doc}`gradient-descent`, will detail how to use these gradients for parameter optimization."

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/back-propagation.md:351
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"关于反向传播在实际神经网络训练中的应用，参见 {doc}`../cnn-expedition/practice-peak/neural-"
"training-basics`。"
msgstr ""
"For the application of backpropagation in practical neural network training, see {doc}`../cnn-expedition/practice-peak/neural-training-basics`."

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/back-propagation.md:357
msgid "参考文献"
msgstr "References"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/back-propagation.md:126
msgid ""
"这里是简化的版本，实际应为 **最大奇异值**（maximum singular value）。对向量（多层梯度）而言，局部放大倍数由 "
"Jacobian 矩阵 $\\frac{\\partial h_{k+1}}{\\partial h_k}$ "
"的最大奇异值给出，它决定了梯度模长经过这一层映射后被放大或缩小的最大倍数。"
msgstr ""
"This is a simplified version; in practice, it refers to the **maximum singular value**. "
"For vectors (multi-layer gradients), the local amplification factor is given by the "
"maximum singular value of the Jacobian matrix $\\frac{\\partial h_{k+1}}{\\partial h_k}$, "
"which determines the maximum factor by which the gradient magnitude is amplified or scaled down after passing through this layer."
